# Lifecycle governance

Follow `AGENTS.md` and `specs/greenfield/INSTRUCTIONS.md` + `ORCHESTRATION_MANIFEST.md` on every chat.

## Gate 2

If `GATE2_APPROVAL.txt` is missing or lacks `[APPROVED: …]`, do not create or edit `backend/go.mod`, `backend/go.sum`, `backend/**/*.go`, or `backend/sql/**`. Refuse and ask for approval. Specs, Docker files, and this rule may be edited.

## Stages

Implement only the current stage. Do not skip Gate 3 (schema + Base62 + Go module) before the coverage command in `backend/`: `go test ./... -count=1 -covermode=atomic -coverpkg=./... -coverprofile=coverage.out`, then `go tool cover -func=coverage.out` with `total:` ≥ 80%. On test failure: fix code, never `t.Skip`, max 3 retries, then stop. Do not start Stage 6.

## Lineage

Append `SDLC_AUDIT_LOG.json` and update `SDLC_METRICS.json` per `INSTRUCTIONS.md`. Do not invent coverage or claim generated files in `specs/scenarios/01-greenfield.md`.

## High impact — halt

Changing SQL tables after Gate 2, adding undeclared direct requirements in `backend/go.mod`, or dropping the 80% / mandatory test bar requires a new human signature. Re-plan to Stage 1 if `PRD.md` or `SYSTEM_DESIGN.md` changes mid-run.

## Frontend

`specs/frontend/` and `20-frontend-react.mdc` may exist. Do not generate `frontend/src/**` or `frontend/package.json` during the Go stages. The client does not change the OpenAPI contract.
